--TEST--
`Revocable` is declared by the compiler and has no registry row, so its name in an `implements` clause answers the card that sits beside its seeding, `rule:classes/revocable-objects`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Post implements Revo<|>cable {
    public function constructor(public string $title) {}
}
--REQUEST--
hover
--EXPECT--
```nvs
interface Revocable
```

An object that can be revoked. After `revoke()`, the object is removed from every `Core\ObjectMap`, `Core\ObjectSet` and `Core\Heap`, and any other use of it throws `RevokedObjectError`.
